.TH FASTRDP-FRONT-CERT 8 "October 2026" "fast-rdp-server" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fastrdp-front-cert \- self-signed front certificate for the fastrdp proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fastrdp-front-cert
.RB [ \-\-if\-missing ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RI [ alias ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes a self-signed certificate and key to
.I /etc/fastrdp/front.crt
and
.I /etc/fastrdp/front.key
(group _fastrdp-proxy, key mode 0640). The subject alternative names are the FQDN
(\fBhostname \-f\fR), the short name and the given aliases (other DNS names clients
use). Clients warn about a self-signed certificate: use it in a lab only and install a
CA certificate (full chain) in production.
.PP
fastrdp-proxy.service runs it with
.B \-\-if\-missing
before every start, so a first start without a certificate gets one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-if\-missing
Do nothing when front.crt or front.key exists.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Replace an existing certificate (e.g. after a rename or for new aliases).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fastrdp-check-host (8)
